<figure class="exhibit" data-exhibit="taxitips" data-src="/data/taxitips.json" id="fig-05">
  <div class="exhibit__bar">
    <span class="mono"><strong>Fig. 05</strong> · what predicts a taxi tip</span>
    <span class="ticks" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="mono">NYC 2023 · real coefficients</span>
  </div>

  <div class="ctl-row" role="group" aria-label="Regression model">
    <button class="btn" type="button" data-model="linear" aria-pressed="true">Linear regression</button>
    <button class="btn" type="button" data-model="lasso" aria-pressed="false">LASSO (λ = 0.01)</button>
    <p class="readout"><span data-ro-view aria-live="polite">…</span></p>
    <noscript><p class="mono">Interactive exhibit requires JavaScript.</p></noscript>
  </div>

  <canvas data-coef height="380" role="img"
    aria-label="Fitted regression coefficients for all 27 features, linear versus LASSO"></canvas>

  <canvas data-ci height="74" role="img"
    aria-label="Cross-validated R squared with 95 percent confidence intervals for both models"
    style="margin-top: 0.6rem"></canvas>

  <table class="mono tx-table" aria-label="Model performance">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>model</th><th>cv R² (95% CI)</th><th>test R²</th><th>RMSE</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody data-metrics><!-- filled from real model results --></tbody>
  </table>

  <figcaption class="figcap mono">
    Real fitted coefficients and metrics from the report, not a simulation.
    Toggle LASSO and watch it zero 15 of 27 features. Cash trips were removed
    before training because cash tips are never logged. RMSE is shown with its
    share of the mean tip.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

